{"timestamp":"2026-08-26T10:07:27.703Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03d89-f9d7-73a1-8ebf-17e6fa377050","call_id":"call_N6v5xj4BDNyXTFIOP5ob4BHV","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"        Add the new computed blocks to the request.\n\n        Args:\n            request_id: The request ID.\n            new_computed_blocks: The new computed blocks just hitting the\n                prefix cache.\n        \"\"\"\n        if request_id not in self.num_cached_block:\n            # A new request.\n            req_blocks = self.req_to_blocks[request_id]\n            assert len(req_blocks) == 0\n            req_blocks.extend(new_computed_blocks)\n            self.num_cached_block[request_id] = len(new_computed_blocks)\n        else:\n            # A running request. Should not have new computed blocks.\n            assert len(new_computed_blocks) == 0\n\n    def allocate_new_blocks(\n        self, request_id: str, num_tokens: int\n    ) -> list[KVCacheBlock]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Allocate new blocks for the request to give it at least `num_tokens`\n        token slots.\n\n        Args:\n            request_id: The request ID.\n            num_tokens: The total number of tokens that need a slot (including\n                tokens that are already allocated).\n\n        Returns:\n            The new allocated blocks.\n        \"\"\"\n        req_blocks = self.req_to_blocks[request_id]\n        num_required_blocks = cdiv(num_tokens, self.block_size)\n        num_new_blocks = num_required_blocks - len(req_blocks)\n        if num_new_blocks <= 0:\n            return []\n        else:\n            if self.block_pool._locality_on():\n                new_blocks = self.block_pool.get_new_blocks_locality(\n                    request_id, num_new_blocks)\n            else:\n                new_blocks = self.block_pool.get_new_blocks(num_new_blocks)\n            req_blocks.extend(new_blocks)\n            return new_blocks\n\n    def cache_blocks(self, request: Request, num_tokens: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Cache the blocks for the request.\n\n        Args:\n            request: The request.\n            num_tokens: The total number of tokens that need to be cached\n                (including tokens that are already cached).\n        \"\"\"\n        num_cached_blocks = self.num_cached_block.get(request.request_id, 0)\n        num_full_blocks = num_tokens // self.block_size\n\n        if num_cached_blocks >= num_full_blocks:\n            return\n\n        self.block_pool.cache_full_blocks(\n            request=request,\n            blocks=self.req_to_blocks[request.request_id],\n            num_cached_blocks=num_cached_blocks,\n            num_full_blocks=num_full_blocks,\n            block_size=self.block_size,\n            kv_cache_group_id=self.kv_cache_group_id,\n        )\n\n        self.num_cached_block[request.request_id] = num_full_blocks\n\n    def free(self, request_id: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Free the blocks for the request.\n\n        Args:\n            request_id: The request ID.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.block_pool._locality_on():\n            self.block_pool.on_request_freed_locality(request_id)\n\n        # Default to [] in case a request is freed (aborted) before alloc.\n        req_blocks = self.req_to_blocks.pop(request_id, [])\n\n        # Free blocks in reverse order so that the tail blocks are\n        # freed first.\n        ordered_blocks = reversed(req_blocks)\n\n        self.block_pool.free_blocks(ordered_blocks)\n        self.num_cached_block.pop(request_id, None)\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def get_num_common_prefix_blocks(self, running_request_id: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Get the number of common prefix blocks for all requests with allocated\n        KV cache.\n\n        Args:\n            running_request_id: The request ID.\n\n# Offline 실행 가이드\n\n`offline_offload_kvweight.py`는 한 process에서 정답, runtime route,\ngenerated token과 TTFT/TPOT를 확인하는 진입점이다. 네 기능 조합 전체는\n[기능 조합 테스트](EXPERIMENT_GUIDE.md), engine 준비와 step 내부 순서는\n[Inference 수행 흐름](INFERENCE_FLOW.md)을 사용한다.\n\n| 방식 | Process/환경 | 자동 판정 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Feature matrix | cell마다 fresh process, 주요 `TIERED_SERVE_*` 정리 | residency, route, semantic answer, optional exact token |\n| 수동 offline | 현재 shell 상속, 임의 config/backend 가능 | semantic answer와 token dump; route는 log에서 확인 |\n\n여러 `--ts-configs`를 한 번에 주면 같은 engine을 reconfigure한다. 독립적인\nA/B에는 config마다 fresh process를 사용한다.\n\n모든 명령은 저장소 루트에서 실행한다.\n\n```bash\ncd /root/projects/tiered-serve\n```\n\n## 0. LD_PRELOAD: CPython frame-stack mmap/munmap 제거\n\nCPython 3.12은 interpreter frame data-stack을 16 KiB 단위로\n`mmap(MAP_ANONYMOUS)`/`munmap`으로 할당·해제한다. vLLM V1의 깊은\nper-piece call chain이 이 경계를 반복적으로 넘어 nsys에서 step당\n수천 회의 `mmap64`/`munmap`을 발생시킨다.\n\n`etc/stack_pool.so`는 `mmap64`/`munmap`을 가로채서 16 KiB chunk를\nfree-list pool로 재사용한다. 반환 시 `memset`으로 zeroing하여\n`MAP_ANONYMOUS`의 zeroed-page 계약을 보존한다.\n\n**모든 실행 명령에 `LD_PRELOAD`를 붙인다.**\n\n```bash\nLD_PRELOAD=/root/projects/tiered-serve/etc/stack_pool.so\n```\n\n`.so` 빌드 방법은 [구조 가이드의 Tips](LANDING_GUIDE.md#6-tips)를\n참고한다.\n\n## 1. 실행 전 확인\n\n[구조 가이드의 preflight](LANDING_GUIDE.md#1-지원-범위와-workspace)를 먼저\n통과해야 한다. 새 shell을 사용하고 이전 실험의 KV codec/layout 설정을\n물려받지 않도록 다음 값을 비운다.\n\n```bash\nunset TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_PRODUCER\nunset TIERED_SERVE_KV_BLOB_STRIDE\nunset TIERED_SERVE_KV_BLOB_SLACK\nunset TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_PREFILL_LOAD\nunset TIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_SIZE_GB\n```\n\nCorrectness 예제는 고정 prompt로 2 tokens를 만들고 `Paris`를 semantic\noracle로 사용한다. Batch 1 full-block KV compression은 logical `D=16`,\ntail `S=1`, physical offset `D+S=17`이므로 dedicated-row request는 17,\nplanner override는 1025를 사용한다.\n\n## 2. 네 기능을 켠 correctness 실행\n\n### 2.1 8B\n\n```bash\nTIERED_SERVE_NUM_WEIGHT_HUGE_PAGE=2 \\\nTIERED_SERVE_N_WEIGHT_BUFFERS=2 \\\nTIERED_SERVE_DEDICATED_KV_BLOC